"rules.nonogram" = "Fill cells to match each row and column clue. Runs appear in order and require at least one empty square between them. Switch between fill and cross-out. Sizes are 5×5, 10×10 and 15×15; generated puzzles have a unique solution.";
"rules.kakuro" = "Fill white cells with digits 1–9. Each horizontal or vertical run uses distinct digits totaling its clue. The upper-right clue runs across; the lower-left clue runs down. Some starting digits are fixed. Player entries are blue; mistakes are not marked. Each puzzle has a unique solution.";
"rules.klotski" = "Slide blocks on a 4×5 board without rotating, overlapping or leaving the board. Move the 2×2 goal block to the bottom center exit. Select and use arrows or swipe a block. Every new board is created by reversible legal moves from a solved position.";
"rules.gomoku" = "Freestyle Gomoku uses a 15×15 board with black moving first. Five or more consecutive stones horizontally, vertically or diagonally win. A full board without a winner is a draw. Renju forbidden-move rules do not apply. Play offline against the computer or locally with two players.";
"rules.reversi" = "Black moves first. A move must bracket opposing discs in at least one direction; all bracketed discs flip. A player with no legal move passes automatically. When neither player can move, the player with more discs wins; equal counts draw.";
"rules.xiangqi" = "Red moves first. Chariots slide orthogonally; horses cannot jump a blocked leg; elephants cannot cross the river or a blocked eye; advisors and generals stay in their palaces. Cannons capture over exactly one screen. Soldiers gain sideways moves after crossing the river and never retreat. Exposing your general or facing the generals is illegal. Checkmate or stalemate loses. Threefold repetition draws, except repeated perpetual check loses for its initiator.";
"rules.banqi" = "Taiwanese dark chess uses a 4×8 board. The first reveal assigns player one’s color. Reveal or move once per turn. Pieces move one orthogonal square and capture equal or lower ranks; a soldier may capture a general, but a general may not capture a soldier. Cannons capture a revealed enemy over exactly one screen. Eliminate the opponent or leave them no legal action to win. Eighty quiet moves draw. The computer never inspects hidden identities.";
"rules.chess" = "Standard chess with white moving first, check safety, castling, en passant and promotion to queen, rook, bishop or knight. You cannot expose your king. Checkmate wins. Stalemate, threefold repetition, fifty moves without a pawn move or capture, and insufficient mating material draw. Choose the promotion piece when prompted.";
"rules.shogi" = "Standard 9×9 shogi. Eligible pieces may promote when moving into, within or out of the far three ranks. Pawns and lances must promote on the last rank; knights on the last two. Captured pieces demote and enter your hand for drops. Double pawns, dead-rank drops and pawn-drop mate are forbidden. Checkmate or no legal move loses. Fourfold repetition draws; perpetual check loses for its initiator.";
"rules.klondike" = "Classic seven-column Klondike. Build descending alternating-color columns; move valid sequences together. Only kings fill empty columns. Build each foundation from ace to king by suit. Choose draw one or three, with unlimited stock recycling. Collect all 52 cards to win. Random deals are not guaranteed solvable.";
"rules.spider" = "Spider uses 104 cards. Build columns down in rank; different suits may connect, but only suited sequences move together. Complete suited king-to-ace runs collect automatically; eight runs win. All columns must be occupied before dealing one card to each column. Choose one, two or four suits.";
"rules.freecell" = "FreeCell uses eight columns, four free cells and four foundations. Build columns down in alternating colors; any card fills an empty column. Each free cell holds one card. Sequence capacity depends on available free cells and empty columns. Build foundations up by suit from ace to king; collect 52 cards to win.";
"rules.pyramid" = "Remove cards not covered by the two cards below. Exposed pairs totaling 13 remove together; jack is 11, queen 12, and king 13. A king removes alone. Pair tableau cards with the waste top too. The stock has one pass. Clear the pyramid to win; no remaining legal move loses.";
"rules.tripeaks" = "Move an exposed card one rank above or below the waste onto it; ace and king connect. Draw from the stock when needed, with one pass only. Clear all three peaks to win. No stock and no legal tableau move loses.";
"rules.snake" = "Turn using the direction buttons. Food grows the snake and increases the score. Immediate reversal is forbidden. Hitting a wall or your body ends the game; filling the board completes it. Difficulty changes board size and speed. Simulation stops while paused or in the background.";
"rules.fallingblocks" = "Seven tetrominoes use a shuffled seven-piece bag. Fill horizontal rows to clear them. Move, rotate either way, hold, soft drop or hard drop. Hold is allowed once per falling piece. Clearing rows increases speed. A blocked spawn or locking above the top ends the game.";
"rules.brickbreaker" = "Drag across the board or use arrow buttons to move the paddle, then launch. Hits damage bricks and score points; hard mode has tougher bricks. Bounce angle depends on where the ball hits the paddle. Each miss costs a life. Clear all bricks to win before losing all three lives.";
